          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-08 11:35:31.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-19916 idl: reserve MGS follower opcodes and flags",
        "message": "LU-19916 idl: reserve MGS follower opcodes and flags\n\nReserve the wire and on-disk values of the MGS follower features, so\nthat they can land before the feature patches:\n- MGS_SET_PARAM (257), with struct mgs_set_param_body and\n  MSPB_REPLAY, for an MGS follower forwarding \"lctl set_param -P\" to\n  MGS0, and an acting MGS leader passing on the ones it took\n- MGS_IR_HANDOVER (258), for an acting MGS leader passing its IR\n  version to MGS0\n- CM_ACTING (0x20) and CM_REPLAYED (0x40) llog marker flags, for the\n  params log records of an acting MGS leader\nOnly the values, the opcode names and the wire checks are added, and\nmgs_mgs_handlers[] is sized to MGS_LAST_OPC, so that an MGS answers\neither opcode with -EOPNOTSUPP rather than looking past the end of\nthe array.  Nothing sets the flags yet.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ibafd6c1868c13a41b5147fb56803f0a8293ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
